WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.490
- I'm here with Blake Shelton,

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:03.340
and on Skype is Cynthia Nixon!

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:04.599
Give it up for 'em!

00:00:04.599 --> 00:00:06.040
(audience cheering)

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.330
(laughs) Good, good clap.

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:08.340
Everyone knows,

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.670
Blake and I, are a little
competitive. Just a little.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.850
He is. I'm really easy going.

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:16.500
Earlier, (chuckles) he even
gave me a wall of champions,

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.300
that displays every person,

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.100
who's beat me, at a game, on this show.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.510
Well, I'm not afraid.

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.010
I'm gonna give Blake a chance,

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:25.360
to get on that wall, right now.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.299
Keyword meaning chance.
- Yes.

00:00:27.299 --> 00:00:28.132
- [Blake] There you go.

00:00:28.132 --> 00:00:29.240
- It's a slim one.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.052
And since Blake and I--
- Read it, girl.

00:00:31.052 --> 00:00:32.700
- Are both big "Golden Girls" fans,

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.348
it's time to play, actually,
"You're Golden GURRRRRL."

00:00:35.348 --> 00:00:37.131
(upbeat music)

00:00:37.131 --> 00:00:40.790
♪ You're golden gurrrrrl ♪

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:43.610
Cynthia has been kind
enough to volunteer to host,

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:44.821
and probably referee.

00:00:44.821 --> 00:00:47.000
Thank you, Cynthia.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.620
Cynthia will read questions
about "The Golden Girls."

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.672
The first person to hit the buzzer

00:00:51.672 --> 00:00:54.110
and answer correctly gets the point.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:56.580
You can steal, if the person is wrong.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.040
Most points wins.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.790
But, there's always a little twist,

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:01.880
in the time of COVID, right?

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.460
So, since we have to stay
apart from each other,

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.570
we're not close enough to hit the buzzer.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.080
So, on his podium, on Blake's
podium, that he gave us.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:12.040
So, we have these hand extenders,

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:13.913
that I will now showcase, as a baton.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.370
Okay, let's do this.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:17.910
I had a shot. Let's do this.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:18.743
First question.

00:01:18.743 --> 00:01:19.950
Please, Cynthia.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:20.860
- Here we go!
- Okay.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:22.360
- What are,

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:23.960
what are the names,

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.520
of all four Golden Girls.
(buzzer rings)

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.145
- (yelling) Wait! What? Wait!

00:01:27.145 --> 00:01:28.278
- I knew where she was getting at.

00:01:28.278 --> 00:01:29.506
- But can't. what do you think?

00:01:29.506 --> 00:01:31.900
So we, so you don't have
to say the whole question?

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.050
- No. Do you know the names?

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:34.000
Do you know all four names?

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.610
- Sophia, Blanche,
(kelly scoffs)

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.570
Rose, and Dorothy.
(bell dings)

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:39.210
- I didn't! I didn't know you couldn't.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.043
But! Okay.

00:01:40.043 --> 00:01:40.876
- What do ya mean you didn't know?

00:01:40.876 --> 00:01:42.638
This is your show, this is--
- I, I didn't, no!

00:01:42.638 --> 00:01:43.480
- This is you TV show!
- I don't make up the games.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:44.313
- [Cynthia] All right.
- I'm not--

00:01:44.313 --> 00:01:45.888
- Right here, on T-K-C-S!

00:01:45.888 --> 00:01:46.985
- You got one down. Four to go!

00:01:46.985 --> 00:01:49.100
- (laughing over announcement) T-K-C-S!

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.330
- I thought that you had to
listen the whole question.

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:52.610
Okay. Fine.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:53.880
- All right, question number two.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:54.790
- Okay.

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:56.000
- What is

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.089
the favorite dessert of the golden girls?

00:01:59.089 --> 00:02:00.270
(buzzers ring simultaneously)
- Oh! Oh!

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.220
Awe, you got that one I think.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:03.213
- Blake?
- Cheesecake!

00:02:03.213 --> 00:02:04.046
- Yes!

00:02:04.046 --> 00:02:04.950
(bell dings)

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.262
That is correct!
(audience cheering)

00:02:06.262 --> 00:02:07.095
- Dammit!

00:02:07.095 --> 00:02:08.354
- All right,

00:02:08.354 --> 00:02:09.687
we've got Blake for two.

00:02:09.687 --> 00:02:11.360
- He can not get on this wall, Cynthia!

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.100
- Okay.
- Okay.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.720
- This is a really hard one.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.830
- Oh, like the last one was simple?

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:17.663
Okay.

00:02:17.663 --> 00:02:18.660
- Rose

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.893
is originally from what small town?

00:02:23.797 --> 00:02:26.165
(laughter in audience)

00:02:26.165 --> 00:02:29.090
- Awe, she says it every episode. (sighs)

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.180
- I have it.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.890
I'm going to let you struggle
with it for a minute,

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.220
but, I do have a hint.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.730
- Okay. I think we need the hint.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.403
- It is also,

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:39.430
the name,

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:40.750
of a snowman,

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.080
who likes warm hugs.
(buzzer ringing)

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.570
- Olaf Minnesota!

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:46.940
- No! That's not right!

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:49.038
- St. Olaf, but the judges Take it!

00:02:49.038 --> 00:02:50.079
- Oh! That's not right!
(bell dinging)

00:02:50.079 --> 00:02:51.562
- Yup.
- What's not right?

00:02:51.562 --> 00:02:52.395
(audience cheering)
- That is--

00:02:52.395 --> 00:02:53.228
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:53.228 --> 00:02:54.920
- That is not close enough, Cynthia.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.310
- What? I--
- This is bull crap!

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.890
- I think it is.
- Olaf!

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:59.410
- The judges accept it.
- St. Olaf!

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:00.860
- St. Olaf? But, he, I.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:01.785
- Hey, anybody can just be Olaf.

00:03:01.785 --> 00:03:02.859
- Everybody knows that he's a saint.

00:03:02.859 --> 00:03:04.008
- But, if you're a saint
Olaf, that's big deal.

00:03:04.008 --> 00:03:05.550
- Everybody knows that he's a saint Olaf.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.070
I don't have to say saint,
you can leave the saint off.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:08.903
I didn't know. (laughs)

00:03:08.903 --> 00:03:10.140
- Okay.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:12.553
The theme song goes:

00:03:12.553 --> 00:03:14.700
" Thank you for being a friend,

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.450
traveled down the road and back again."

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.035
What is the next line?

00:03:19.035 --> 00:03:20.297
(buzzer ringing)
- Oh!

00:03:20.297 --> 00:03:21.527
- "Your heart is true,
- Damn!

00:03:21.527 --> 00:03:23.051
- "You're a pal and a confidant."

00:03:23.051 --> 00:03:23.884
(bell dings)
(audience wooing)

00:03:23.884 --> 00:03:26.360
- Damn!
(audience cheering)

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.030
You're so quick at the, it's this hand!

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:30.940
I'm saying, I'm saying flag on the play.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.590
- I'm afraid Blake has got three.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:35.050
- Oh my gosh!

00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:36.650
Whatever!
- He's unbeatable.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:38.008
- I think, that I'm calling--
- I'm afraid that Blake

00:03:38.008 --> 00:03:39.010
- I think that this--
- Is going on the Wall,

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:39.843
of Champions.

00:03:39.843 --> 00:03:41.400
- I-- (sighs)
- Thank you, Cynthia.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.800
Thank you.
- So, and the winner's Blake!

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.230
Watch Ratched, everybody!

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:47.290
- Yes!
- Yes!

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.580
Watch it!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.350
- Okay. Do we have a picture
of Blake, for the wall?

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:53.183
Oh God.

00:03:53.183 --> 00:03:54.130
- Oh, thank you.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:55.610
Okay. No, hold on. Let me see it first.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:56.710
Let me just. Do you have a little?

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:58.920
Can I have a, Oh, that's so interesting.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.601
That just in case--
- How 'bout the Sasquatch?

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:01.434
You done with the Sasquatch?
- Just in case,

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:02.267
the pigs are flying,

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:04.297
and hell is freezing
over, and you beat me,

00:04:04.297 --> 00:04:06.590
(audience laughing)
these are...

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.270
Okay. here we go.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:11.110
I put a little tears on your face,

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:12.900
'cause I, I actually let you win,

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:13.984
just so you can be on the wall.

00:04:13.984 --> 00:04:15.670
- In your defense, you have been drinking.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:17.753
- (laughs) I have.
- Yup.

